\subsection{Subtyping and Parametricity}\label{sec:subtyping-parametricity}

The combination of subtyping and parametric polymorphism raises subtle issues. In System~F$_{<:}$, parametricity is weakened: a polymorphic function $\forall \alpha <: T.\, \alpha \to \alpha$ is not fully parametric because $\alpha$ ranges only over subtypes of $T$.

\begin{insight}
The tension between subtyping and parametricity is fundamental. Subtyping introduces a non-trivial lattice structure on types, while parametricity requires uniform behavior across all types. The resolution in practice is to use subtyping for nominal hierarchies (class-based) and parametricity for generic programming (type-parameterized), keeping the two mechanisms separate.
\end{insight}

